            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a puncture, then the Telugu for to mend."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: రహదారి",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రహదారి — rahadāri — \"a highway; a main road\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "జాతీయ రహదారి మీద వాహనాలు వేగంగా వెళ్తాయి. jātīya rahadāri mīda vāhanālu vēgaṅgā veḷtāyi. Vehicles go fast on the national highway."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "జాతీయ రహదారి (rahadāri) is a national highway. దారి alone is any way or path."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రహదారి (rahadāri) is a compound whose second part is దారి, \"a way, a road\"; the first part is usually traced to Persian rāh, \"a road\", and the whole is read as \"the main road\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
