          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దూసుకుపోవు (dūsukupōvu) is a Telugu compound: its first part has an origin that is not settled, and its second part is the native పోవు, \"to go\" (DEDR 4572)."
